  <prompt>Apply punch row A44.5 (the H7/task-142 half of A30's sentinel contract that A38's 4h budget could not close within its `KvSecretsPopulation/**` scope). Row-by-row shape: (a) grep-verify current repo state BEFORE applying — locate `H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler`, the H6 handler, `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()`, and `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` KV-ref site; (b) READ master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` FR-39 ordered-credential migration pattern (brought in via A35) and MIRROR it — do NOT invent a parallel pattern; (c) apply the three-part fix per the escalation record: (1) FR-39-style ordered credential provider on H7/H6 (`Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` for secret-free envs; client-secret fallback for backwards compat), (2) make the Bicep `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref conditional on the secret-free flag (mirror A38b's `requireSecretFreeIdentity` param pattern in `customer.bicep`), (3) relax `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` to accept empty `ClientSecret` when the ordered credential is MI-FIC-first (STILL fail-fast on invalid credential-provider chain); (d) add unit + integration tests asserting both Model 1 (shared L2 Worker + shared UAMI) and Model 2 (per-customer L2 Worker + per-stamp UAMI) code paths; (e) run build + tests + Bicep regen (`customer.json`/`platform-controlplane.json` if module changed); (f) amend punch list annotations. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE L2 Worker credential-seam specialist + FR-39 ordered-credential migration expert + Bicep KV-ref conditional-gating author. Expert in: L2 control-plane Worker boot chain + `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` fail-fast semantics; master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl` MI-branch + ordered secret-free credential (brought in via A35 as the reference implementation to mirror); FR-39 pluggable credential seam contract (`Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` + `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast, per §10.2 live contract); A38a's `ficOmitSecretNames`/`OmitCanonicalNames` seam pattern (extend, don't parallel); A38b's `requireSecretFreeIdentity` Bicep param pattern in `customer.bicep` (mirror for `controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep`); the §9.1 sentinel-pathology contract (empty = signal; NEVER a sentinel in the credential slot — opaque `AADSTS7000215`); Model 1 shared-Worker+shared-UAMI vs Model 2 per-customer-Worker+per-stamp-UAMI topologies (per Wave G-1 task 101, task 029 slot-swap fix); the A30 sentinel contract's H7/task-142 half (task 142 wired `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref UNCONDITIONALLY — A44.5 closes it). PRE-MERGE state awareness: A35 has landed on this branch (deps declare it); direct-read master's pattern from post-merge tree BEFORE mirroring assumed shape.</role>

  <goal>H7 (`H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler`) + H6 handler use FR-39-style ordered credential provider (MI-FIC first for secret-free envs; client-secret fallback for backwards compat) mirroring master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl` pattern brought in by A35 — VERIFIED by grep for `Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` in the handler code path + zero `AuthType=ClientSecret` construction on the secret-free branch. `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref is CONDITIONAL on a secret-free flag (mirror A38b's `requireSecretFreeIdentity` param pattern in `customer.bicep`) — grep-verified: the KV-ref appears only inside the flag-guarded branch. `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` accepts empty `ClientSecret` when the ordered credential provider is MI-FIC-first (grep: presence of ordered-credential check gating the empty-secret allowance); still fail-fasts on invalid provider chain (unit test asserts). L2 Worker boots successfully on secret-free env with `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret=""` (no boot-loop; no §9.1 sentinel) — proven by integration test (`WebApplicationFactory` or equivalent harness) OR by contract-test on the `Validate()` boundary + credential-factory boundary combined. Model 1 (shared-Worker+shared-UAMI, one credential-chain per env) and Model 2 (per-customer-Worker+per-stamp-UAMI, per-customer credential-chain) code paths BOTH explicitly asserted by distinct tests. Unit + integration tests assert: (a) MI-FIC-first credential chain on secret-free env; (b) client-secret fallback on pre-migration env; (c) `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` accepts empty secret under MI-FIC mode; (d) Worker boot succeeds on secret-free env; (e) Model 1 vs Model 2 code paths both covered. Existing task-130 (A42) + task-142 tests PRESERVED (extend, not replace). If the Bicep module changed, `customer.json` + `platform-controlplane.json` regenerated. `dotnet build` succeeds across affected projects (`Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core` + `Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker` + tests). Punch list row A44.5 annotated with `last_known_status_after_execution` in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Punch row A44.5 is the NEW row that task 205a's A38 execution record proposed on 2026-08-25 (peer escalation, owner approved) as the H7/task-142 half of A30's sentinel contract — the half that A38's 4h budget and `KvSecretsPopulation/**` scope could not close. Evidence: H7 (`H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler`) and H6 handler CONSUME `BFF-API-ClientSecret` as their own client-credentials Dataverse auth; task 142 wired `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` → KV-ref UNCONDITIONALLY in `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep`; `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` fail-fasts the whole L2 Worker boot when the secret is empty. On a secret-free env (§6.5 resolution record prong 1: never-create/seed/restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret`) the Worker therefore BOOT-LOOPS — or, worse, invites a §9.1 sentinel value into the slot (the exact pathology this whole re-scope exists to prevent). A44.5 mirrors master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl` FR-39 ordered-credential migration pattern (brought in via A35, verified per remediation plan §1 fact (a): master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` has the MI branch + secret-free ordered credential; the raw `AuthType=ClientSecret` connection string was replaced at auth-v4 task 022). The seam is the SAME class as A38a's `ficOmitSecretNames` — but for the Worker's OWN auth, not for KV secrets it writes. A38b (task 205g) established the Bicep `requireSecretFreeIdentity` param pattern in `customer.bicep`; A44.5 mirrors it in `controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep`. A42 (task 205b) is concurrently reconciling task-130's FIC creation for BFF app-reg — a DIFFERENT app-reg (L2 UAMI-based) — so no code-surface overlap, but shared FR-39 ordered-credential pattern.</background>
