  <constraints>
    <constraint source="A44.5 row spec">MUST mirror master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl` migration pattern (secret-free ordered credential brought in via A35). Do NOT invent a parallel pattern — grep + READ the master file first (Step 1) and structurally MIRROR it into H7/H6.</constraint>
    <constraint source="A44.5 row spec">MUST make `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref conditional in `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` (mirror A38b's `requireSecretFreeIdentity` param pattern in `customer.bicep`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="A44.5 row spec">MUST NOT delete `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref outright — backwards compat requires it on pre-migration envs (prong 3 of the §6.5 record: unmigrated envs still resolve the secret). Conditional flag defaults to preserve current behavior.</constraint>
    <constraint source="A44.5 row spec">MUST relax `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` to accept empty `ClientSecret` WHEN the ordered credential provider is MI-FIC-first. MUST NOT relax when a secret-based provider is required. Two distinct code paths, both fail-fast on invalid provider-chain configuration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10.2 live contract + A38a">MUST use FR-39 pattern (`Graph__Credentials__Order__0=ManagedIdentityFederated` + `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` fail-fast) consistent with §10.2 live contract and A38a's `ficOmitSecretNames`/`OmitCanonicalNames` seam. Extend the same seam shape — do NOT introduce a parallel naming convention. Suggested option name: `WorkerFicMode` or `WorkerCredentialProvider` (verify against existing `EnvVarValuesOptions` conventions in Step 1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="A44.5 row spec + design.md D2/D3">Model 1 shared-UAMI vs Model 2 per-stamp-UAMI: acceptance MUST cover BOTH explicitly with distinct tests. Model 1 = shared L2 Worker (one per environment), shared UAMI (per task 029 slot-swap fix + shared BFF UAMI), one credential-chain config per env. Model 2 = per-customer L2 Worker (per Wave G-1 task 101), per-stamp UAMI, per-customer credential-chain config.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §9.1 + §6.5 resolution prong 1">MUST NOT re-open the §9.1 sentinel pathology — on secret-free envs, empty is the SIGNAL. NEVER a sentinel value in the credential slot (opaque `AADSTS7000215`). Positive migration markers go in a provisioning-state field or KV tag (A38a scope) — NEVER the `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` slot.</constraint>
