  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, Fable @ xhigh; auth-tagged + tests/**-modifying override — code-review + adr-check UNCONDITIONAL at Step 9.5). Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` A44.5 row + A38 execution record block (lines 76-108) + A38a/b/c row descriptions. Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-remediation-plan.md` §5 item 3 (silent-failure catalog for H7/task-142 surface) + §7 (sequencing) + §8 (effort). Read `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` full record (approved 2026-08-25). Read root CLAUDE.md §6.5 + §8.5 + §10. Read project CLAUDE.md §Applicable ADRs + §MUST rules.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep-verify current repo state BEFORE applying">Grep + read: (a) locate `H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler.cs` full path + the H6 handler sibling (verify H6's exact class name; row says "H6 handler" — resolve). (b) READ `EnvVarValuesOptions.cs` and locate `Validate()` — record the exact fail-fast condition for empty `ClientSecret`. (c) READ `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` and locate the `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref site (task-142 wiring, unconditional). (d) READ master's `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` (post-A35 merge) — this is the FR-39 ordered-credential pattern to MIRROR; record the exact option-name convention, factory shape, provider-chain ordering, and Validate-boundary. (e) READ `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` for A38b's `requireSecretFreeIdentity` param pattern (if A38b landed) — record the exact param name + conditional shape. (f) Grep task-142 test names + task-130 test names — record for preservation check in Step 9. (g) Verify whether `customer.json` + `platform-controlplane.json` are committed compiled artifacts. Record everything in scratchpad table before any edit.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Verify A35 landed + master pattern present">Confirm A35 landed (grep for A4 in `.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md` — presence of "Amendment A4" heading; grep for `-FicOnly` occurrences in `scripts/Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1` — expect 16 per remediation plan §1). Confirm master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs` MI-branch present. If A35 has NOT landed → STOP + escalate (dependency not met).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Design mirror — extract the FR-39 ordered-credential shape from master">From Step 1(d)'s read of `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs`, extract: (a) option-class shape + name convention (whether `Graph__Credentials__Order__N` list or a discriminated enum); (b) the credential-factory pattern (interface + implementations); (c) the Validate boundary (what makes an empty secret ACCEPTABLE vs FAIL-FAST); (d) how MI-FIC vs client-secret fallback is chained. Draft the mirroring plan for H7/H6 + `EnvVarValuesOptions` in scratchpad — cite the master file's line numbers you're mirroring. Do NOT edit code yet.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint (after ~3 steps of read/design)">Run `context-handoff`.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Apply — H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler (part 1 of 3)">Edit `H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler.cs` to consume the FR-39 ordered-credential provider (per master's pattern, mirrored). Preserve backwards compat: if the ordered chain resolves to client-secret, existing behavior is unchanged. Extend the H6 handler with the same seam (H6 shares the L2 Worker Dataverse auth surface per row A44.5). If a shared credential-factory helper is warranted (both handlers consume it), author it in `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EnvVarValues/` or a shared `Credentials/` sub-namespace — cite A44.5 + §11 justification in the new file header.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Apply — EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate() relaxation (part 2 of 3)">Edit `EnvVarValuesOptions.cs` `Validate()` — accept empty `ClientSecret` ONLY when the ordered credential provider is MI-FIC-first. STILL fail-fast on: (a) invalid provider-chain configuration, (b) empty `ClientSecret` when a secret-based provider is required (prong-3 unmigrated env), (c) any other required-field violation currently enforced. Do NOT weaken any existing invariant.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Apply — Bicep KV-ref conditional (part 3 of 3)">Edit `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` — introduce a `requireSecretFreeIdentity` bool param (default `false` — preserves current behavior); wrap the `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` KV-ref app-setting in an `if (!requireSecretFreeIdentity)` branch (or the equivalent Bicep conditional shape used in `customer.bicep` per A38b). If A38b's param name differs, ADOPT A38b's name for consistency. Do NOT delete the KV-ref outright — conditional only.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Regenerate compiled Bicep JSON (if committed)">If `customer.json` / `platform-controlplane.json` are committed compiled artifacts (Step 1(g)), regenerate via the project's Bicep-build convention (typically `bicep build` or `az bicep build`). Grep-confirm the regenerated JSON reflects the new conditional shape.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Add tests + preserve existing">Add unit + integration tests under `tests/unit/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Handlers/EnvVarValues/` asserting: (a) MI-FIC-first credential chain on secret-free env; (b) client-secret fallback on pre-migration env; (c) `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` accepts empty secret under MI-FIC mode; (d) `Validate()` still fail-fasts on invalid provider chain + on empty secret when secret-based provider required; (e) Worker boot succeeds on secret-free env (via `WebApplicationFactory` or equivalent — if unavailable, contract-test the credential-factory + `Validate()` boundaries in combination + document in test summary that full-boot proof lands post-App-Service in E2E T4 per remediation plan §5 item 2 SF-4); (f) Model 1 shared-Worker+shared-UAMI code path (one credential-chain config per env); (g) Model 2 per-customer-Worker+per-stamp-UAMI code path (per-customer credential-chain config). Preserve ALL existing task-142 + task-130 test names verified in Step 1(f) — run them BEFORE and AFTER to prove no regression.</step>
