  <notes>Justification (root CLAUDE.md §11 three-question — required per project CLAUDE.md §11):

  **Existing** — The L2 Worker's Dataverse client-credentials auth surface exists in `H7DataverseEnvVarValuesHandler` + the H6 handler, wired via `EnvVarValuesOptions` (task-142). The master pattern being mirrored (`DataverseServiceClientImpl` FR-39 ordered credential) exists in `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/` (brought in via A35, per remediation plan §1 fact (a) — verified by direct read). The A38a `ficOmitSecretNames`/`OmitCanonicalNames` FR-39 seam exists in `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/` (task-126). The A38b `requireSecretFreeIdentity` Bicep param pattern exists (or is in-flight) in `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep`.

  **Extension** — A44.5 extends (does NOT parallel) three existing patterns: (1) master's `DataverseServiceClientImpl` FR-39 ordered credential shape, mirrored into H7/H6; (2) A38a's `ficOmitSecretNames`/`OmitCanonicalNames` seam shape, extended for Worker's own auth (not KV writes); (3) A38b's `requireSecretFreeIdentity` Bicep param pattern, mirrored into `controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep`. If A42 (task 205b) landed a shared credential-factory helper, A44.5 consumes it rather than authoring a parallel factory (per escalation trigger `a42-shared-helper-diverges`). New files (test files; possibly a Worker-scoped credential-factory helper if not already provided by A42) each cite A44.5 in file header + this justification.

  **Cost-of-doing-nothing** — Concrete failure modes without A44.5, all verified evidence in the escalation record (peer 2026-08-25):

  1. **Boot-loop** — on a secret-free env under §6.5 resolution prong 1 (never-create/seed/restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret`), `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` is empty; `EnvVarValuesOptions.Validate()` fail-fasts the whole L2 Worker boot; every fresh secret-free customer environment cannot start its L2 Worker. This is the exit-134-class silent boot-abort catalogued in remediation plan §8 ("cost of NOT executing: … BFF that fails one of three ways: boot-abort … boots-but-dead … silently WRONG").

  2. **§9.1 sentinel pathology invited** — operators or scripts, faced with the boot-loop, will write a non-empty placeholder into `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` to unblock the Worker → opaque `AADSTS7000215` at first Dataverse call (auth-v4 §9.1 anti-pattern; catalogued in remediation plan §5 SF-16). The sentinel absorbs a broken credential chain with every health signal green — strictly worse than the boot-loop.

  3. **Prong 1 becomes unenforceable** — every fresh secret-free env under prong 1 has two silent options (boot-loop OR sentinel) — the §6.5 resolution record's central invariant ("never CREATE/seed/restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret`") is effectively unenforceable for L2 Worker's own credential slot without A44.5.

  4. **task-186 blocks conditionally** — task 186 targets `spaarke-hosted-model2` (Q9 verified) which uses the existing shared L2 Worker. If the existing Worker already has `BFF-API-ClientSecret` in KV (rollback copy under Q3 Path A until 2026-11-23), boot-loop is DEFERRED but the Worker cannot be re-deployed on secret-free config without A44.5. First greenfield Model 2 stamp attempted after A38-A42 land will boot-loop or invite a sentinel without A44.5.

  5. **A30 sentinel contract remains half-open** — A38 closed the H4 half of A30's sentinel contract (KV secrets it writes); the H7/task-142 half (L2 Worker's OWN auth consumption) is exactly what A44.5 exists to close. Without A44.5, A30 remains half-open indefinitely; every future customer inherits the trap.

  Recommendation (per row A44.5 source + remediation plan §7): land in same bundle as A38a+A38b+A38c for complete omit-set contract closure. A44.5 is disjoint from A38a/b/c on code surface (EnvVarValues/** vs KvSecretsPopulation/** vs customer.bicep vs scripts/*.ps1), so it is parallel-safe within the bundle.

  Blast radius: every future customer's L2 Worker boot chain on a secret-free env. Fable-tier assignment (per §8.5 cost posture) and FULL rigor (per §8.5 override for auth-tagged + tests/**-modifying) are BOTH mandatory.</notes>

